From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:45:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 004/111] Restore the previous session, including unsaved
 changes

The editor reopens the tabs of the last session: files, untitled
documents, unsaved changes, cursor, scroll, Markdown view and the active
tab. Unsaved text is kept as drafts in ~/.local/state/cosmic-edit/session
(folder 0700, files 0600, atomic writes), at most 3 s after an edit, on
tab changes and on quit, so a crash loses only the last seconds.

Closing the window keeps unsaved work in the drafts instead of asking.
Closing a single tab still asks, and discarding deletes its draft. A
missing file with a draft comes back as unsaved; a file changed on disk
after its draft keeps the draft and logs it. A corrupt session file is
kept as session.ron.bad and the editor starts empty. Only one editor
uses the session at a time.

Settings > Session > "Restore previous session" (on by default). Off
behaves as before and deletes the stored session.

